findings.proposed_change:
lemma nonconstant_inv {k K : Type*} [DivisionRing k] [DivisionRing K] (c : k →+* K) {a : K}
    (ha : a ∉ Set.range c) : a⁻¹ ∉ Set.range c
The proof stays the same: `rintro ⟨b,hb⟩; exact ha ⟨b⁻¹, by rw [map_inv₀, hb, inv_inv]⟩`. `map_inv₀` only needs a `MonoidWithZeroHomClass` between two `GroupWithZero`s, which `→+*` between division rings provides. The one call site, `nonconstant_inv (curveFieldScalar sC) ha` in RelativeAmpleness.lean, still elaborates because `k := ℂ` is inferred from `c`. Degenerate case: `a = 0` gives `a⁻¹ = 0 = c 0`, which is excluded by `ha` both before and after the change.
